Hi Anindya,

May I suggest that you start with building web applications within R first without rApache? There are two ways to do this:

1. You can use the Rook package which gives you a foundation for dealing with all aspects of web application development. Later on when you are happy with your Rook application, then you can deploy it to rapache. Here's a tutorial on Rook <http://anythingbutrbitrary.blogspot.com/2012/12/a-simple-web-application-using-rook.html>, and here's a blog post <http://jeffreyhorner.tumblr.com/post/27861973339/deploy-rook-apps-with-rapache-part-i> about deploying Rook apps on rApache.

2. You can write your applications with the shiny package <http://www.rstudio.com/shiny/>. It's still early days for shiny, but it shows lots of promise.

All the best,

Jeff

